Integration increment: tutor UI + Space Invaders removal.

Key decisions / why:
- Single-transaction ingest in controllers/paper.py: a persisted Paper always
  has both chunks and an analysis. analyze() runs BEFORE commit so a failed
  analysis aborts the whole upload (no half-ingested papers). Single source of
  truth, no repair/migration paths.
- One conversation per (paper, session); append_turn persists BOTH user and
  assistant messages in one commit so stored history can never be half-written.
- Session scoping is the only access boundary (anonymous app): every read is
  WHERE session_id = current; cross-session access returns 404 (indistinguishable
  from "not found") to avoid leaking existence.

pgvector bug (important): services/embeddings._search_pgvector used
PaperChunk.embedding.op('<=>')(cast(list, Vector(dims))). The resulting distance
expression inherited the EmbeddingVector TypeDecorator as its result type, so the
scalar float distance was passed through process_result_value (list(value)),
raising "'float' object is not subscriptable" and silently falling back to the
in-Python NumPy ranking. The native DB path was effectively dead. Fix: cast BOTH
operands to pgvector Vector(dims) and pin op('<=>', return_type=Float) so the
distance decodes as a float. Verified against docker pgvector/pgvector:pg16 with
the migration applied: the DB path returns grounded citations with no fallback
warning. pgvector's .cosine_distance() comparator is NOT available on the
TypeDecorator-wrapped column, which is why explicit casts are used.

frontend/src/lib/ was being swallowed by the Python `lib/` rule in .gitignore;
added an explicit negation so the spec-mandated lib/api.ts is tracked.

jest-dom matchers: tsc (strict, includes src/**) needs the type augmentation, so
src/vitest-env.d.ts references @testing-library/jest-dom and tests/setup.ts
imports the /vitest entry (jest-dom v6).

